<section id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Cell segmentation.</h4>

<div id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS4.SSS0.Px2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In a Terminal-Bench cell-segmentation task, a refactor deletes helper
functions before compaction. The summary retains the known error and
backup identity but omits the exact edit commands. With summary and
memory available, the actor rereads both files, restores the helpers,
and passes all nine verifier tests (Figure <a href="#S3.F5" title="Figure 5 ‣ Cell segmentation. ‣ 3.4 Case studies ‣ 3 Experiments ‣ Remory: Learning Residual Memoryfor Context Compaction" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>). The repair
illustrates complementary roles for summary, memory, and retrieval;
it does not establish which omitted details came from memory.</p>
