<section id="S4" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">4 </span>Related Work</h2>

<div id="S4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Agent memory often combines summaries with retrieval. ReadAgent pairs
episode gists with original passages, while MemGPT separates working
and archival memory <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib18" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lee et al., 2024</a>; <a href="#bib.bib26" title="" class="ltx_ref">Packer et al., 2023</a>)</cite>.
ReSum uses periodic summaries for long-horizon search; AgentFold learns
multi-scale context management within agent
trajectories <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wu et al., 2025</a>; <a href="#bib.bib34" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ye et al., 2025</a>)</cite>.
<span id="S4.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Remory</span> keeps the textual checkpoint and retrieval interface, and learns
an additional continuous representation conditioned on the checkpoint.</p>
</div>
<div id="S4.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.p2.1" class="ltx_p">AutoCompressors, Gist Tokens, and ICAE learn continuous representations
of longer text <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Chevalier et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib23" title="" class="ltx_ref">Mu et al., 2023</a>; <a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Ge et al., 2024</a>)</cite>.
LCLMs scale encoder–decoder compression and support selective expansion
of compressed segments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib19" title="" class="ltx_ref">Li et al., 2026a</a>)</cite>.
Distribution matching provides a behavioral criterion for prompt
compression <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib32" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wingate et al., 2022</a>)</cite>; recurrence and memory tokens
retain information across segments <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib8" title="" class="ltx_ref">Dai et al., 2019</a>; <a href="#bib.bib4" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bulatov et al., 2022</a>)</cite>.
Our objective applies this predictive criterion to the information gap
left by a summary, training the supplement through a frozen actor’s
continuation predictions.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S5" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">5 </span>Conclusion</h2>

<div id="S5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S5.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S5.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Remory</span> learns a bounded memory supplement for contextual compaction.
The summary provides a readable account of prior work, soft tokens
carry additional predictive information, and retrieval supplies exact
records when needed. Reconstruction followed by summary-conditioned
continuation trains this interface while leaving the actor unchanged.
Improved source attribution, higher agent scores, and preferred next
actions support the usefulness of this residual formulation.</p>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
